   127	def main(grid: np.ndarray) -> np.ndarray:
   128	    """
   129	    Queue hollow outlines along the bottom by increasing internal marker count and fill each cavity with its majority marker color.
   130	
   131	    Input structure:
   132	    - The background is dominant.
   133	    - Foreground consists of monochrome closed outline components plus isolated one-pixel markers of one or more colors.
   134	    - Some markers lie inside outline-enclosed regions and some lie outside as distractors.
   135	
   136	    Rule:
   137	    - Remove every marker and clear the canvas.
   138	    - For each closed outline, count only the markers inside its enclosed region, keep the outline's original shape and color, and fill that enclosed region with the unique majority marker color found there.
   139	    - Reposition the resulting filled outlines left-to-right in increasing internal-marker-count order, with their bottom edges aligned to the grid bottom and exactly one blank column between consecutive outlines.
